      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>The issue for me with using Kickstarter as a preorder outlet for a product that&#39;s already almost finished is that it seems to create unrealistic expectations for companies who use it as a way to raise capital, since customers seem to get the impression from the former group that creating something takes much less time and money than it actually does, which then opens the latter group to unfair criticisms. Granted, this issue wouldn&#39;t be such an issue if companies were always open about saying when they already have partial development/funding completed, but until then it&#39;s still an issue.</p><p>With this specifically I admit I&#39;ve been reading the &quot;RPG companies usually have a PDF of the RPG right after the Kickstarter&#39;s done&quot; comments people have been making and wondering what would happen then to RPG creators who used KS because they actually needed the funding to be able to then properly create the PDF.</p>",
      "actions_summary": [
